# Products whose ML-DSA-65 release signature (<rpm>.mldsa65.sig) is required,
# one product name per line. Read by scripts/verify/admit-release.sh.
#
# A second signature that may be left out protects nothing: whoever can forge
# the Ed25519 signature simply does not attach it. For a product listed here a
# missing signature refuses the release. A line that is not exactly a product
# name (`podup # since 2.0`, `Podup`) refuses the run as a malformed local file,
# so a typo cannot switch the requirement off. A comment takes a line of its own.
# Empty today: no key exists yet, and a product enters this list once one of
# its releases was verified with both signatures by the real pipeline.
